; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR SIMPLE-CALC 5  -  five-digit decimal floating point   (VM1 @ $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; A rewrite from the ground up of Calc-Float-v05 (none of its code is reused).
; Needs firmware V0061.22 or later (DIVMAX $5C, PRINTSTR $C1, GETSTR $C2);
; built and verified against V0061.30.
;
;   > 2+3*4            = 20          left to right, like a pocket calculator
;   > *2               = 40          a line starting + * / uses the last answer
;   > -2.5*4           = -10         a leading - is a negative number
;   > 1/7              = 0.14286     rounded, not truncated
;   > 60000*60000      = 3600000000
;   > 1/60000/60000    = 2.7778E-10
;   > 5/0              = Err         the last answer is kept
;   > 5+             = ?           so is it after a typing mistake
;   Enter on an empty line quits.  x also means times.
;
; NUMBERS are sign, mantissa and decimal exponent: (-1)^s * m * 10^e, with m
; one 16-bit register (0..65535) - about five significant digits.  Every number
; typed or computed is ROUNDED HALF-UP to the largest mantissa that fits, so
; 99999 reads as 100000, 999*999 = 998000 (998001 needs six digits), and
; 6083.02 is held as 6083.0.  Exponents run -90..+90: past +90 is Err, below
; -90 is 0.  Plain display for integers of up to 10 digits and up to 10
; decimal places; d.dddd E x otherwise.
;
; ALL THE ARITHMETIC IS NATIVE STELLAR OPS - no software multiply or divide:
;   *    MULTXY -> 32-bit MA, then DIVMAX the MA by 10 until it fits in 16
;        bits, rounding on the last digit dropped.
;   /    DIVXY for the whole part, then one digit at a time (MULTXY r*10,
;        DIVMAX by the divisor) until the next digit would not fit; it rounds.
;   + -  both mantissas left-justified, the bigger number first, then the first
;        scaled up by 10^d (d <= 4) or by 10^4 with the second scaled down
;        (d = 5..8), added or subtracted in 32 bits held in RA:RB.
;
; FIRMWARE FINDINGS made building this (V0061.30, simulator):
;   $50 ADDXYZ - when RX + RY passes $FFFF the carry lands in the byte BEFORE
;        the destination register (FFF0 + 0020 -> R3: R3 = 0010, R2 0020->0021).
;        This program never lets ADDXYZ wrap.
;   $54 ADDMXMY / $55 SUBMXMY with D=4 lose the top byte of the result
;        (B2D05E00 + 00012345 -> 00D18145), so 32-bit sums use two registers.
;   $35 COPYIMXA / $36 COPYIAMX refuse 4 bytes of the MA (error $0C) though
;        COMMANDS says 1-4; $37 / $38 with D=4 work and are used here.
;
; REGISTERS.  R0 input character.  R1 R2 R3 the running answer (sign,
; mantissa, exponent+$80).  R4 R5 R6 the next number.  R7 R8 scratch.  R9 the
; operator.  RA:RB a 32-bit value.  RC input cursor.  RD error flag.  RE
; scratch.  RF ten.  Call depth 2 at most (main -> ADD -> POW10).
;
; DATA past the end marker: banner and strings $4C00-$4D2F, last answer $4D40,
; scratch $4D50, digit buffer $4D60, input line $4E00 (to the end of the block).
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/simplecalc5_verify.py, real V0061.30 image,
; cold boot): an exact-fraction model applies the same rounding rule and the
; printed answer must match it character for character - 57 set cases + 400 random expressions, 0 wrong.
; Slowest line measured, 1/60000/60000, is ~160,000 1802 instructions.
;
; HARDWARE-VERIFIED on the Elf2K, 2026-09-24, on firmware V0061.33 - Craig: "works
; very well".
;
; 477 STELLAR commands, $4000-$453F (1344 bytes of code).
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START                              Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A                    Ten, used everywhere
; D 4005 11 0E 0D 40    LOADXI R14 0D40                    The last answer starts as +0 (the pre-pass does not clear RAM)
; D 4009 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 400D 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4011 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 4015 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4019 32 0E 00 80    COPYMX2I R14 0080
; D 401D 11 0E 0C 00    LOADXI R14 0C00
; D 4021 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       The banner
; PROMPT:
; D 4023 11 0E 0D 00    LOADXI R14 0D00
; D 4027 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       >
; D 4029 11 0C 0E 00    LOADXI R12 0E00
; D 402D 11 0D 0E 00    LOADXI R13 0E00
; D 4031 C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     Read a line (echoed; backspace works)
; D 4033 11 0C 0E 00    LOADXI R12 0E00                    Back to the start of it
; D 4037 BD 01 61       CALL SKIPSP
; D 403A 8C 00          TESTXZ R0                          An empty line quits
; D 403C A0 01 58       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 403F 86 00 00 2B    TESTXI R0 002B                     A line that starts with + * / carries on
; D 4043 A0 00 68       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 4046 86 00 00 2A    TESTXI R0 002A                     from the last answer
; D 404A A0 00 68       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 404D 86 00 00 2F    TESTXI R0 002F
; D 4051 A0 00 68       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 4054 BD 01 75       CALL PARSE                         The first number -> R4 R5 R6
; D 4057 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10                         No digits: not a number
; D 4059 A0 01 40       IFTRUEI SYNERR
; D 405C 23 00 41       COPYXY R4 -> R1                    It becomes the running answer R1 R2 R3
; D 405F 23 00 52       COPYXY R5 -> R2
; D 4062 23 00 63       COPYXY R6 -> R3
; D 4065 B0 00 7D       GAL OPLOOP
; USEANS:
; D 4068 11 0E 0D 40    LOADXI R14 0D40                    Load the last answer
; D 406C 39 02 E1       COPYMXY M(R14) -> R1
; D 406F 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4073 39 02 E2       COPYMXY M(R14) -> R2
; D 4076 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 407A 39 02 E3       COPYMXY M(R14) -> R3
; OPLOOP:
; D 407D BD 01 61       CALL SKIPSP
; D 4080 8C 00          TESTXZ R0                          End of the line: show the answer
; D 4082 A0 01 1C       IFTRUEI SHOW
; D 4085 23 00 09       COPYXY R0 -> R9                    R9 = the operator
; D 4088 86 09 00 2B    TESTXI R9 002B
; D 408C A0 00 AE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 408F 86 09 00 2D    TESTXI R9 002D
; D 4093 A0 00 AE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 4096 86 09 00 2A    TESTXI R9 002A
; D 409A A0 00 AE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 409D 86 09 00 78    TESTXI R9 0078                     x works as times too
; D 40A1 A0 00 AE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 40A4 86 09 00 2F    TESTXI R9 002F
; D 40A8 A0 00 AE       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 40AB B0 01 40       GAL SYNERR                         Anything else is a mistake
; OPOK:
; D 40AE 42 0C          INCX R12                           Past the operator
; D 40B0 BD 01 61       CALL SKIPSP
; D 40B3 BD 01 75       CALL PARSE                         The next number -> R4 R5 R6
; D 40B6 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 40B8 A0 01 40       IFTRUEI SYNERR
; D 40BB 11 0D 00 00    LOADXI R13 0000                    No error yet
; D 40BF 86 09 00 2B    TESTXI R9 002B
; D 40C3 A0 00 F3       IFTRUEI DOADD
; D 40C6 86 09 00 2D    TESTXI R9 002D
; D 40CA A0 00 E3       IFTRUEI DOSUB
; D 40CD BD 02 48       CALL XSIGN                         Times and divide: the sign is the exclusive-or
; D 40D0 86 09 00 2F    TESTXI R9 002F
; D 40D4 A0 00 DD       IFTRUEI DODIV
; D 40D7 BD 02 5E       CALL MUL
; D 40DA B0 00 F6       GAL AFTER
; DODIV:
; D 40DD BD 02 7A       CALL DIV
; D 40E0 B0 00 F6       GAL AFTER
; DOSUB:
; D 40E3 8C 04          TESTXZ R4                          Subtract: flip the second number's sign and add
; D 40E5 A0 00 EF       IFTRUEI SUB1
; D 40E8 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; D 40EC B0 00 F3       GAL DOADD
; SUB1:
; D 40EF 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001
; DOADD:
; D 40F3 BD 03 00       CALL ADD
; AFTER:
; D 40F6 8C 0D          TESTXZ R13                         Divide by zero?
; D 40F8 A1 01 49       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 40FB 11 0E 00 DA    LOADXI R14 00DA                    Exponent past +90: too big
; D 40FF 89 E3          TESTLXY R14 < R3
; D 4101 A0 01 49       IFTRUEI MATHERR
; D 4104 11 0E 00 26    LOADXI R14 0026                    Below -90: call it zero
; D 4108 89 3E          TESTLXY R3 < R14
; D 410A A1 00 7D       IFFALSEI OPLOOP
; D 410D 11 01 00 00    LOADXI R1 0000
; D 4111 11 02 00 00    LOADXI R2 0000
; D 4115 11 03 00 80    LOADXI R3 0080
; D 4119 B0 00 7D       GAL OPLOOP
; SHOW:
; D 411C BD 04 4C       CALL NSTRIP                        Canonical (a lone typed number may end in zeros)
; D 411F 11 0E 0D 40    LOADXI R14 0D40                    Keep it as the last answer
; D 4123 3A 02 1E       COPYXMY R1 -> M(R14)
; D 4126 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 412A 3A 02 2E       COPYXMY R2 -> M(R14)
; D 412D 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4131 3A 02 3E       COPYXMY R3 -> M(R14)
; D 4134 11 0E 0D 08    LOADXI R14 0D08
; D 4138 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                        =
; D 413A BD 04 6E       CALL PRINTNUM
; D 413D B0 00 23       GAL PROMPT
; SYNERR:
; D 4140 11 0E 0D 18    LOADXI R14 0D18
; D 4144 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                        = ?  (the last answer is kept)
; D 4146 B0 00 23       GAL PROMPT
; MATHERR:
; D 4149 11 0E 0D 08    LOADXI R14 0D08
; D 414D C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 414F 11 0E 0D 10    LOADXI R14 0D10
; D 4153 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       Err
; D 4155 B0 00 23       GAL PROMPT
; QUIT:
; D 4158 11 0E 0D 20    LOADXI R14 0D20
; D 415C C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 415E F0 00 00       BREAK                              End of program
; SKIPSP:
; D 4161 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 4165 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 4167 86 00 00 20    TESTXI R0 0020
; D 416B A1 01 73       IFFALSEI SKR
; D 416E 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4170 B0 01 61       GAL SKIPSP
; SKR:
; D 4173 BE 00          RETURN
; PARSE:
; D 4175 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; D 4179 11 05 00 00    LOADXI R5 0000
; D 417D 11 06 00 80    LOADXI R6 0080
; D 4181 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; D 4185 11 0A 00 00    LOADXI R10 0000
; D 4189 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000
; D 418D 11 0D 00 00    LOADXI R13 0000
; D 4191 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 4195 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 4197 86 00 00 2D    TESTXI R0 002D                     A leading minus
; D 419B A1 01 A4       IFFALSEI PLOOP
; D 419E 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001
; D 41A2 42 0C          INCX R12
; PLOOP:
; D 41A4 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 41A8 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 41AA 86 00 00 2E    TESTXI R0 002E
; D 41AE A1 01 BF       IFFALSEI PDIG
; D 41B1 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          A second point ends the number
; D 41B3 A1 02 19       IFFALSEI PEND
; D 41B6 11 08 00 01    LOADXI R8 0001                     Digits from here on are fraction
; D 41BA 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 41BC B0 01 A4       GAL PLOOP
; PDIG:
; D 41BF 53 00 00 30    SUBXI R0 0030                      A digit is '0'..'9': c-'0' < 10
; D 41C3 89 0F          TESTLXY R0 < R15
; D 41C5 A1 02 19       IFFALSEI PEND
; D 41C8 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 41CA 11 0A 00 01    LOADXI R10 0001                    Seen a digit
; D 41CE 23 00 07       COPYXY R0 -> R7                    R7 = the digit
; D 41D1 8C 0B          TESTXZ R11                         Mantissa already full?
; D 41D3 A1 02 0F       IFFALSEI PDROP
; D 41D6 11 0E 19 98    LOADXI R14 1998                    m*10+d fits if m <= 6552
; D 41DA 88 E5          TESTGXY R14 >= R5
; D 41DC A0 01 FE       IFTRUEI PACC
; D 41DF 11 0E 19 99    LOADXI R14 1999                    or if m = 6553 and d <= 5
; D 41E3 87 5E          TESTXY R5 = R14
; D 41E5 A1 01 F4       IFFALSEI PFULL
; D 41E8 11 0E 00 05    LOADXI R14 0005
; D 41EC 88 E7          TESTGXY R14 >= R7
; D 41EE A0 01 FE       IFTRUEI PACC
; D 41F1 B0 01 F4       GAL PFULL
; PFULL:
; D 41F4 11 0B 00 01    LOADXI R11 0001                    Full: this digit decides the rounding
; D 41F8 23 00 7D       COPYXY R7 -> R13
; D 41FB B0 02 0F       GAL PDROP
; PACC:
; D 41FE 4A 5F          MULTXY R5 * R15                    m = m*10 + d
; D 4200 21 15          COPYAX MA -> R5
; D 4202 50 57 05       ADDXYZ R5 + R7 -> R5
; D 4205 8C 08          TESTXZ R8
; D 4207 A0 01 A4       IFTRUEI PLOOP
; D 420A 43 06          DECX R6                            After the point each digit is a tenth
; D 420C B0 01 A4       GAL PLOOP
; PDROP:
; D 420F 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          A dropped digit before the point is a x10
; D 4211 A1 01 A4       IFFALSEI PLOOP
; D 4214 42 06          INCX R6
; D 4216 B0 01 A4       GAL PLOOP
; PEND:
; D 4219 8C 0B          TESTXZ R11                         Anything dropped?
; D 421B A0 02 39       IFTRUEI PZERO
; D 421E 11 07 00 04    LOADXI R7 0004
; D 4222 89 7D          TESTLXY R7 < R13                   First dropped digit 5 or more: round up
; D 4224 A1 02 39       IFFALSEI PZERO
; D 4227 86 05 FF FF    TESTXI R5 FFFF                     Round up: 65535 would become 65536,
; D 422B A1 02 37       IFFALSEI RIP
; D 422E 11 05 19 9A    LOADXI R5 199A                     which does not fit - 6554 x 10 instead
; D 4232 42 06          INCX R6
; D 4234 B0 02 39       GAL PZERO
; RIP:
; D 4237 42 05          INCX R5
; PZERO:
; D 4239 8C 05          TESTXZ R5                          Zero is always +0 x 10^0
; D 423B A1 02 46       IFFALSEI PRET
; D 423E 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; D 4242 11 06 00 80    LOADXI R6 0080
; PRET:
; D 4246 BE 00          RETURN
; XSIGN:
; D 4248 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 424A A0 02 5C       IFTRUEI XRET
; D 424D 8C 01          TESTXZ R1
; D 424F A0 02 58       IFTRUEI XNEG
; D 4252 11 01 00 00    LOADXI R1 0000
; D 4256 BE 00          RETURN
; XNEG:
; D 4258 11 01 00 01    LOADXI R1 0001
; XRET:
; D 425C BE 00          RETURN
; MUL:
; D 425E 50 36 03       ADDXYZ R3 + R6 -> R3               Exponents add (both biased, so take one bias off)
; D 4261 11 0E 00 80    LOADXI R14 0080
; D 4265 89 3E          TESTLXY R3 < R14
; D 4267 A1 02 71       IFFALSEI MUL1
; D 426A 11 03 00 1C    LOADXI R3 001C                     Far below -90: will come out as zero
; D 426E B0 02 75       GAL MUL2
; MUL1:
; D 4271 53 03 00 80    SUBXI R3 0080
; MUL2:
; D 4275 4A 25          MULTXY R2 * R5                     The 32-bit product, in the MA
; D 4277 B0 04 19       GAL NORMMA                         Normalise it (NORMMA returns to main)
; DIV:
; D 427A 8C 05          TESTXZ R5
; D 427C A1 02 85       IFFALSEI DIV1
; D 427F 11 0D 00 01    LOADXI R13 0001                    Divide by zero
; D 4283 BE 00          RETURN
; DIV1:
; D 4285 52 03 00 80    ADDXI R3 0080                      Exponents subtract: e1 - e2, kept biased
; D 4289 89 36          TESTLXY R3 < R6
; D 428B A1 02 95       IFFALSEI DIV2
; D 428E 11 03 00 1C    LOADXI R3 001C                     Far below -90: will come out as zero
; D 4292 B0 02 98       GAL DIV3
; DIV2:
; D 4295 51 36 03       SUBXYZ R3 - R6 -> R3
; DIV3:
; D 4298 4D 25          DIVXY R2 / R5                      The whole part
; D 429A 25             COPYMAA
; D 429B 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11                  RB = quotient so far
; D 429D 27             COPYREMA
; D 429E 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10                  RA = remainder
; DLOOP:
; D 42A0 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10                         Nothing left over: exact
; D 42A2 A0 02 FA       IFTRUEI DDONE
; D 42A5 4A AF          MULTXY R10 * R15                   Next digit: remainder x 10
; D 42A7 5C 05          DIVMAX MA / R5                     divided by the divisor
; D 42A9 25             COPYMAA
; D 42AA 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7                   R7 = the digit
; D 42AC 27             COPYREMA
; D 42AD 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8                   R8 = the new remainder
; D 42AF 11 0E 19 98    LOADXI R14 1998                    m*10+d fits if m <= 6552
; D 42B3 88 EB          TESTGXY R14 >= R11
; D 42B5 A0 02 EB       IFTRUEI DACC
; D 42B8 11 0E 19 99    LOADXI R14 1999                    or if m = 6553 and d <= 5
; D 42BC 87 BE          TESTXY R11 = R14
; D 42BE A1 02 CD       IFFALSEI DRND
; D 42C1 11 0E 00 05    LOADXI R14 0005
; D 42C5 88 E7          TESTGXY R14 >= R7
; D 42C7 A0 02 EB       IFTRUEI DACC
; D 42CA B0 02 CD       GAL DRND
; DRND:
; D 42CD 11 0E 00 04    LOADXI R14 0004                    Full: the digit that did not fit rounds
; D 42D1 89 E7          TESTLXY R14 < R7
; D 42D3 A1 02 FA       IFFALSEI DDONE
; D 42D6 86 0B FF FF    TESTXI R11 FFFF                    Round up: 65535 would become 65536,
; D 42DA A1 02 E6       IFFALSEI RID
; D 42DD 11 0B 19 9A    LOADXI R11 199A                    which does not fit - 6554 x 10 instead
; D 42E1 42 03          INCX R3
; D 42E3 B0 02 FA       GAL DDONE
; RID:
; D 42E6 42 0B          INCX R11
; D 42E8 B0 02 FA       GAL DDONE
; DACC:
; D 42EB 4A BF          MULTXY R11 * R15                   q = q*10 + digit
; D 42ED 21 1B          COPYAX MA -> R11
; D 42EF 50 B7 0B       ADDXYZ R11 + R7 -> R11
; D 42F2 23 00 8A       COPYXY R8 -> R10
; D 42F5 43 03          DECX R3                            and one more decimal place
; D 42F7 B0 02 A0       GAL DLOOP
; DDONE:
; D 42FA 23 00 B2       COPYXY R11 -> R2
; D 42FD B0 04 4C       GAL NSTRIP                         Take off trailing zeros (NSTRIP returns to main)
; ADD:
; D 4300 8C 05          TESTXZ R5                          Adding zero
; D 4302 A1 03 07       IFFALSEI ADD1
; D 4305 BE 00          RETURN
; ADD1:
; D 4307 8C 02          TESTXZ R2                          Zero plus B is B
; D 4309 A1 03 17       IFFALSEI AJA
; D 430C 23 00 41       COPYXY R4 -> R1
; D 430F 23 00 52       COPYXY R5 -> R2
; D 4312 23 00 63       COPYXY R6 -> R3
; D 4315 BE 00          RETURN
; AJA:
; D 4317 11 0E 19 99    LOADXI R14 1999                    Left-justify A: x10 while it still fits
; D 431B 88 E2          TESTGXY R14 >= R2
; D 431D A1 03 29       IFFALSEI AJB
; D 4320 4A 2F          MULTXY R2 * R15
; D 4322 21 12          COPYAX MA -> R2
; D 4324 43 03          DECX R3
; D 4326 B0 03 17       GAL AJA
; AJB:
; D 4329 11 0E 19 99    LOADXI R14 1999                    and B
; D 432D 88 E5          TESTGXY R14 >= R5
; D 432F A1 03 3B       IFFALSEI AORD
; D 4332 4A 5F          MULTXY R5 * R15
; D 4334 21 15          COPYAX MA -> R5
; D 4336 43 06          DECX R6
; D 4338 B0 03 29       GAL AJB
; AORD:
; D 433B 89 36          TESTLXY R3 < R6                    Larger magnitude first: bigger exponent,
; D 433D A0 03 4A       IFTRUEI ASWAP
; D 4340 87 36          TESTXY R3 = R6
; D 4342 A1 03 65       IFFALSEI AGO
; D 4345 89 25          TESTLXY R2 < R5                    or same exponent and bigger mantissa
; D 4347 A1 03 65       IFFALSEI AGO
; ASWAP:
; D 434A 23 00 17       COPYXY R1 -> R7
; D 434D 23 00 41       COPYXY R4 -> R1
; D 4350 23 00 74       COPYXY R7 -> R4
; D 4353 23 00 27       COPYXY R2 -> R7
; D 4356 23 00 52       COPYXY R5 -> R2
; D 4359 23 00 75       COPYXY R7 -> R5
; D 435C 23 00 37       COPYXY R3 -> R7
; D 435F 23 00 63       COPYXY R6 -> R3
; D 4362 23 00 76       COPYXY R7 -> R6
; AGO:
; D 4365 51 36 08       SUBXYZ R3 - R6 -> R8               R8 = d, how far apart the exponents are
; D 4368 11 0E 00 08    LOADXI R14 0008
; D 436C 89 E8          TESTLXY R14 < R8                   9 or more: B is below the rounding digit
; D 436E A1 03 74       IFFALSEI ANEAR
; D 4371 B0 04 4C       GAL NSTRIP                         so the answer is A
; ANEAR:
; D 4374 11 0E 00 04    LOADXI R14 0004
; D 4378 89 E8          TESTLXY R14 < R8
; D 437A A0 03 95       IFTRUEI AFAR
; D 437D BD 03 F0       CALL POW10                         d <= 4: A x 10^d, exactly, in 32 bits
; D 4380 4A 29          MULTXY R2 * R9
; D 4382 2B             COPYMAH
; D 4383 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10
; D 4385 25             COPYMAA
; D 4386 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 4388 23 00 57       COPYXY R5 -> R7                    B as it is
; D 438B 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000                     nothing dropped
; D 438F 23 00 63       COPYXY R6 -> R3                    and the answer has B's exponent
; D 4392 B0 03 B4       GAL ACOMB
; AFAR:
; D 4395 53 08 00 04    SUBXI R8 0004                      d = 5..8: A x 10^4, B / 10^(d-4)
; D 4399 BD 03 F0       CALL POW10
; D 439C 4D 59          DIVXY R5 / R9
; D 439E 25             COPYMAA
; D 439F 21 07          COPYAX Acc -> R7                   R7 = B scaled down
; D 43A1 27             COPYREMA
; D 43A2 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8                   R8 = what that dropped (only zero/non-zero matters)
; D 43A4 11 09 27 10    LOADXI R9 2710
; D 43A8 4A 29          MULTXY R2 * R9
; D 43AA 2B             COPYMAH
; D 43AB 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10
; D 43AD 25             COPYMAA
; D 43AE 21 0B          COPYAX Acc -> R11
; D 43B0 53 03 00 04    SUBXI R3 0004
; ACOMB:
; D 43B4 87 14          TESTXY R1 = R4                     Same signs add, different signs subtract
; D 43B6 A1 03 D5       IFFALSEI ASUBW
; D 43B9 11 0E FF FF    LOADXI R14 FFFF                    RA:RB += R7 - never let ADDXYZ wrap
; D 43BD 51 E7 0E       SUBXYZ R14 - R7 -> R14
; D 43C0 89 EB          TESTLXY R14 < R11                  Carry if RB > FFFF - R7
; D 43C2 A1 03 CF       IFFALSEI AADD
; D 43C5 51 BE 0B       SUBXYZ R11 - R14 -> R11            RB - (FFFF - R7) - 1 is the low word
; D 43C8 43 0B          DECX R11
; D 43CA 42 0A          INCX R10                           and carry one
; D 43CC B0 04 04       GAL NORMW
; AADD:
; D 43CF 50 B7 0B       ADDXYZ R11 + R7 -> R11
; D 43D2 B0 04 04       GAL NORMW
; ASUBW:
; D 43D5 89 B7          TESTLXY R11 < R7                   RA:RB -= R7: borrow?
; D 43D7 A1 03 DC       IFFALSEI AS1
; D 43DA 43 0A          DECX R10
; AS1:
; D 43DC 51 B7 0B       SUBXYZ R11 - R7 -> R11
; D 43DF 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          If B lost digits, take one more off
; D 43E1 A0 04 04       IFTRUEI NORMW
; D 43E4 8C 0B          TESTXZ R11
; D 43E6 A1 03 EB       IFFALSEI AS2
; D 43E9 43 0A          DECX R10
; AS2:
